I'm currently (on iOS 4) requesting not to participate in
"multitasking", so the app can behave in the traditional way that has
worked for a year now (save and quit, restore when started again).

What users get if I manage to not just save and quit:

- Elegance.
- The performance gain might be noticeable on older devices, and you
might preserve battery (both are always scarce on mobile devices).
- By opting out of "multitasking" I think I also lose the ability to
start background tasks, in which I could let hearse do its thing when
the user is not playing (this currently happens during gameplay).

